# The spec tree and the source material it is written against are TRACKED.
#
# `projects` and `requirements` were both ignored here until 2026-08-14. That is why a
# completed CMS spec tree — 5 capabilities, 17 units — was deleted with no way to recover
# it: `git add` on a unit was a silent no-op, so nothing was ever committed.
#
# It also breaks the framework's own gates. `ba-capability-split` and `ba-unit-split`
# verify their inputs with `git cat-file -e origin/main:projects/...`; if `projects/` can
# never reach main, those gates can never open, for any project.
#
# And `pm-spec-review` in `intake` mode reviews the intake *against* `requirements/` —
# it refuses outright when that folder is absent, so a reviewer working from a fresh
# clone needs it present.
#
# Do not re-add either path. If a specific document must not be distributed, exclude that
# file by name and record why.

# Local git worktrees created by tooling — not part of the spec tree
.claude/worktrees/

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Resources pulled in from acx_product_management for local reference/reuse —
# not part of this repo's own tracked spec tree.
